      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first log house in the settlement was built in 1824, marking the start of Macedonia’s rural community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.macedonia.oh.us/community/macedonia-history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the early 1800s, Henry Woods discovered a stream he called Indian Run, which became a focal point for early settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.macedonia.oh.us/community/macedonia-history",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Abraham Cranmer bought 90 acres near Indian Run at the intersection of Jenkins and N., helping shape the town’s early layout.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.macedonia.oh.us/community/macedonia-history",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Macedonia Historical Society preserves the town’s story, guiding visitors through dusty aisles of local artifacts.",
